## Update Documentation After Changes

After creating or modifying any of the items below, update the corresponding docs IN THE SAME SESSION — never defer.

| Change | What to update |
|---|---|
| New / changed DB function | Domain doc only (e.g. `requirements/Reward.md`, `CS_Conversations.md`). Do NOT touch `INDEX_FUNCTION.md`. Regenerate `REGISTRY_SUPABASE.md` via the `registry-regenerate` skill so future greps see the new name. |
| New table or schema change | Domain doc (e.g. `Reward.md`) AND `requirements/domains/<domain>.md` (until that file is merged in Phase 6 of `agent-context-architecture.md`). Regenerate `REGISTRY_SUPABASE.md` via the `registry-regenerate` skill. |
| New / changed Supabase edge function | Domain doc + `requirements/REGISTRY_RENDER.md` (add/move/delete the `E:` line). |
| New / changed pg_cron job | Domain doc + `requirements/REGISTRY_RENDER.md` (`C:` line). |
| New / changed PGMQ queue | Domain doc + `requirements/REGISTRY_RENDER.md` (`Q:` line). |
| New / changed Render service | Domain doc + `requirements/REGISTRY_RENDER.md` (`R:` line). |
| New / changed Inngest function or MCP tool | Domain doc + `REGISTRY_RENDER.md` if it has a public surface. |
| New domain or undocumented tables | Create `requirements/<Domain>.md`, add entry to `requirements/domains/_index.md`. |
| CS tables/functions | Use `cs_` prefix, `CS_*.md` docs. |
| Feature behavior change with an active Feature Guide | Update `requirements/feature-docs/<feature>.md` (only `rewards.md` is currently Active — see `requirements/feature-docs/INDEX.md`). |
| **Any of the above (final step)** | **Append a one-line entry to `requirements/CHANGELOG.md` under today's date, linking the domain MD where full detail lives.** |

### Why both the domain doc AND `REGISTRY_RENDER.md`

`REGISTRY_RENDER.md` is hand-maintained and serves as the single grep target for "what edge functions / queues / crons / Render services exist." If you add a function but don't update the registry, it becomes invisible to future agents that grep first. The registry's value collapses without this discipline.

`REGISTRY_SUPABASE.md` is **not** hand-edited — it is regenerated from the live DB by the `registry-regenerate` skill. Run that skill at the close of any task that added, renamed, or dropped a function or table so future greps find the right name.

### Changelog Entry (final step, every task that changed docs)

After updating the domain doc(s) and any registries, append one bullet to `requirements/CHANGELOG.md` summarizing the change. This is part of the same task — no separate approval needed.

- Newest date at top. Add a new `## YYYY-MM-DD` section if today's date isn't there yet.
- Format: `**<Domain>** — <one-sentence summary>. See \`requirements/<Doc>.md\` §<Section>.`
- One bullet per change. Bug fixes that change behavior are in scope; pure refactors and doc-only edits are not.
- Never duplicate detail in the changelog — the linked MD is the source of truth.

### About `INDEX_FUNCTION.md` (DEPRECATED — do not read or write)

This 100KB index is **deprecated and unmaintained**. Its role is replaced by `requirements/REGISTRY_SUPABASE.md`, which is:
- Generated on demand from `pg_proc` / `information_schema` by `scripts/regen_registry_supabase.sql` via the `registry-regenerate` skill
- Smaller, grep-friendly, domain-grouped
- Refreshed at the close of any task that changed the schema or a function signature

Hard rules:
- Never full-read `INDEX_FUNCTION.md`.
- Never edit `INDEX_FUNCTION.md` by hand.
- To look up a function: grep `REGISTRY_SUPABASE.md`, then verify the signature via Supabase MCP (`pg_proc`).
- To regenerate the registry on demand: use the `registry-regenerate` skill.

### The "No Domain Doc" Rule

If no domain doc exists for the tables you're touching: create `requirements/<Domain>.md` and add a one-line entry to `requirements/domains/_index.md` as part of the current task. Applies even for pre-existing undocumented tables.

### How to update the domain index

`requirements/domains/_index.md` is a **pointer index** — one row per domain pointing at the per-domain file (and, post-Phase-6, at the authoritative `<Domain>.md`). Keep each row to: domain name · keywords · file path. Do not embed schemas or function signatures here; those live in the per-domain file (or the authoritative doc) and in `REGISTRY_SUPABASE.md`.

### Writing Conciseness (token-aware)

Index files, requirement docs, and registries become input tokens in future threads. Write the minimum that carries full meaning:
- Per-domain index row: keywords + file path. Nothing else.
- Domain docs: schema + business rules + function signatures. No narrative filler.
- Registry entries: one line per item. No prose.
- Never add "comprehensive," "robust," or any modifier that doesn't add information.

### Feature Guide Updates

Only when behavior visible to testers/CS/marketing changes AND the feature has an Active guide (currently only `rewards.md`). Skip for refactors, perf optimizations, bugfixes restoring documented behavior. Do NOT update archived drafts under `requirements/archive/feature-docs-draft/`. For writing rules, see `13-feature-guide-writing.mdc`.

### Rules

- Doc + registry updates are part of the task — no separate approval needed.
- CS domains: prefix filenames with `CS_`.
- Keep entries factual — no aspirational descriptions.
- A task that touched an edge fn / queue / cron / Render service is NOT done until `REGISTRY_RENDER.md` reflects the change.
